### Expensio Backend - Phase 1 Manual Testing Suite (.http / REST Client)
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5001

### 1. Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/health

### 2. Email Sign Up
# @name signup
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/email/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alan.doe@example.com",
  "password": "Password@123",
  "firstName": "Alan",
  "lastName": "Doe"
}

### 3. Verify Email OTP (Copy the challengeId and OTP from the terminal output)
# Note: In the terminal running the backend, find:
# "[DEV SIMULATION] Email to alan.doe@example.com: Your Expensio verification code is: XXXXXX"
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/verification/email/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "challengeId": "{{signup.response.body.data.challengeId}}",
  "otp": "123456"
}

### 4. Mobile OTP Start (Sends SMS via Twilio / Dev Simulation)
# @name mobileStart
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/mobile/otp/start
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "+919876543210"
}

### 5. Verify Mobile OTP
# Find the OTP in the terminal output:
# "[DEV SIMULATION] SMS to +919876543210: Your Expensio verification code is: XXXXXX"
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/verification/mobile/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "challengeId": "{{mobileStart.response.body.data.challengeId}}",
  "otp": "123456"
}

### 6. Email Login
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/email/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alan.doe@example.com",
  "password": "Password@123"
}

### 7. Google OAuth Login (Dev Mock)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/google
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idToken": "mock_google_dev_test"
}

### 8. Refresh Token Rotation
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{login.response.body.data.refreshToken}}"
}

### 9. Forgot Password Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/password/forgot
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alan.doe@example.com"
}

### 10. Logout
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{login.response.body.data.refreshToken}}"
}

